The goldens are this port's output. Three of the five differ from the reference
dazzle, all in ways that predate the spec arena and the location pinning — they
were re-checked against /usr/local/bin/dazzle while the goldens were blessed,
and the port's side of each is identical with the arena ON, with it OFF, and on
the commit before either landed.

  useloss  the reference additionally reports two ArcEngine diagnostics
           ("reference in architecture to non-existent ID") — the architecture
           transform the port keeps only as a GATE (see the file header of
           dazzle/DssslSpecEventHandler.scaly).
  noparts  same family: the reference adds "element DSSSL-SPECIFICATION
           unfinished in meta-DTD".
  extspec  the missingPart anchor of a SPECID reference: reference 12:0,
           port 12:23. The port anchors at the attribute value, the reference
           at the element. Diagnostic-only, recorded in COMPLETENESS.md.

Everything these fixtures are FOR — that the location survives its parse and
still resolves to the right file, line and column — is identical to the
reference in all five, and extok (a runtime error resolving through an external
specification's chunk table into an entity-expanded .scm) is character-for-
character equal.
